Part A: Theoretical Questions

1. Explain what DevOps Engineering is. How does it differ
from traditional development and operations roles?

  Ans : DevOps ( Development & Operation ) is a culture and set of practises that make automated , Reliable , more faster , less bug issue , fast feedback software development life cycle . DevOps Enginnering is the practical and real life problem solution system that used DevOps system . 

  Mainly traditonal development and operation roles do not have Collaboration between development and operations team .In other hand now Devops combined development and operations team together and make more faster , less bug free software . autometed all proess(by useing some tools) of software development life cycle 

2. Describe how DevOps fits into the Software Development
Life Cycle (SDLC). Mention at least three SDLC phases
where DevOps adds value.

  Ans :  DevOps mainly conmbined development and operation team together also give looping workflow in SDLC . We know there is some process in SDLC( plan > build > test > deploy > monitor ) and DevOps add something more process like (plan > code > build > test > release > deploy > operate > monitor)

